00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
The Chronicles of Narnia: The Voyage of the Dawn Treader is a 2010 high fantasy adventure film directed by Michael Apted from a screenplay by Christopher Markus, Stephen McFeely, and Michael
Petroni, based on the 1952 novel The Voyage of the Dawn Treader, the third published and fifth chronological novel in the children's book series The Chronicles of Narnia by C.

12
00:32:43,636 --> 00:32:49,636
The sequel to The Chronicles of Narnia: Prince Caspian (2008), it is the third
and final installment in The Chronicles of Narnia film series.

13
00:35:27,272 --> 00:35:33,272
It is the only film in the series not to be distributed by Walt Disney
Studios Motion Pictures, which was replaced by 20th Century Fox.

14
00:38:10,909 --> 00:38:16,909
However, Disney would eventually own the rights to all the films in the series
following the acquisition of 21st Century Fox by Disney in 2019.

15
00:40:54,545 --> 00:41:00,545
Georgie Henley, Skandar Keynes, Ben Barnes and Tilda Swinton reprise their
roles from the second film, with Will Poulter joining the cast.

16
00:43:38,181 --> 00:43:44,181
The film is set three Narnian years after the events of Prince Caspian.

17
00:46:21,818 --> 00:46:27,818
The two youngest Pevensie siblings, Edmund and Lucy, are transported
back to Narnia along with their cousin Eustace Scrubb.

18
00:49:05,454 --> 00:49:11,454
They join the new king of Narnia, Caspian, in his quest to rescue seven lost
lords and save Narnia from a corrupting evil on a dark island.

19
00:51:49,090 --> 00:51:55,090
Each character is tested as they journey to the
home of Aslan at the world's far end.

20
00:54:32,727 --> 00:54:38,727
Development on the film began in 2007, while Prince
Caspian was still in production.

21
00:57:16,363 --> 00:57:22,363
Filming was supposed to take place in Malta, the Czech Republic, and Iceland in 2008
with Michael Apted as its new director, for a planned release in 2009.

22
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
However, production was halted after a budgetary dispute between Walden Media and Walt Disney Pictures following Prince Caspian's performance at the
box office, resulting in Disney's departing the production and being replaced by 20th Century Fox under its Fox 2000 Pictures label.

23
01:02:43,636 --> 01:02:49,636
Later, filming took place in Australia and New Zealand in 2009.

24
01:05:27,272 --> 01:05:33,272
It is the only film in the series to be released in 3D.

25
01:08:10,909 --> 01:08:16,909
The Chronicles of Narnia: The Voyage of the Dawn Treader premiered on November 30, 2010, selected for the Royal Film
Performance, before it was theatrically released on December 9 in the United Kingdom and December 10 in the United States.

26
01:10:54,545 --> 01:11:00,545
The film received mixed reviews from critics.

27
01:13:38,181 --> 01:13:44,181
It was a moderate success at the box office, grossing over $415.6 million
worldwide and becoming 20th Century Fox's highest-grossing film in 2010.

28
01:16:21,818 --> 01:16:27,818
The song "There's a Place for Us" by Carrie Underwood was nominated
for Best Original Song at the 68th Golden Globe Awards.

29
